#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A report each time Claude finishes a reply: read it in a tmux popup or in the browser.

    claude-reports              open the picker (meant for: tmux display-popup -E)
    claude-reports hook         Stop hook: write the report (hook JSON on stdin)
    claude-reports list         print reports, newest unread first (used by the picker)
    claude-reports show ID      print a report's markdown
    claude-reports open ID      open a report in the browser (served by `serve`, with buttons:
                                go to pane, mark read, kill session)
    claude-reports open-pane PANE
                                open the report of the Claude session in a tmux pane
                                (bind e run-shell -b "claude-reports open-pane '#{pane_id}'")
    claude-reports resume ID    go to the session: jump to its pane, or resume it in tmux
    claude-reports toggle ID    mark read / unread
    claude-reports delete ID    delete a report
    claude-reports serve        the HTTP server behind the browser pages (127.0.0.1 only;
                                started on demand, exits when idle)
    claude-reports read-all     mark every report read
    claude-reports count [--tmux]
                                number of unread reports; --tmux prints a status-line segment
                                (nothing when there are none)

One report per session, rewritten after every reply: your latest prompt, Claude's final
reply to it, the files it changed on the way, and your earlier prompts. A reply counts as
read when it arrives in the pane you are looking at (tmux focus events). Stored as
<session id>.md and .json in $CLAUDE_REPORTS_DIR (default $XDG_STATE_HOME/claude-reports),
pruned after $CLAUDE_REPORTS_KEEP_DAYS days (default 14).

$CLAUDE_REPORTS_PORT      server port (default 47823)
$CLAUDE_REPORTS_IDLE      seconds without requests before the server exits (default 1800)
$CLAUDE_REPORTS_BROWSER   browser command (default google-chrome-stable, else xdg-open)
$CLAUDE_REPORTS_FOCUS     command run after opening, e.g. to raise the browser window;
                          {title} is replaced by the page title (shell-quoted)
$CLAUDE_REPORTS_ASSETS    live-preview.nvim's static/ folder, for markdown-it rendering
                          (default: its lazy.nvim path; falls back to python-markdown)
$CLAUDE_REPORTS_RESUME    resume command (default $CLAUDE_SESSIONS_RESUME, else
                          "claude --resume {id}"); used when claude-sessions is not installed
"""

